drm/imagination: mark BXM-4-64 MC1 36.56.104.183 (Allwinner A733) as supported (a7a-fedora)

Upstream master's support table (1c21f240fbc1 "Warn or error on unsupported hardware") lists 36.52.104.182 and
36.53.104.796 only; anything else fails the probe with -ENODEV unless powervr.exp_hw_support=1 is set, which
also prints an "unsupported hardware" warning. The A733's core has its firmware in linux-firmware
(rogue_36.56.104.183_v1.fw, Fedora ships it) and its device entry in Mesa 26.2, so "supported" is the honest
state; a modprobe.d line would be one more file every image and RPM has to carry.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
@@ -533,6 +533,9 @@
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(33, 15, 11, 3):
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 52, 104, 182):
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 53, 104, 796):
+	/* a7a: BXM-4-64 MC1 in the Allwinner A733 (Radxa Cubie A7A/A7Z). Its firmware
+	 * rogue_36.56.104.183_v1.fw is in linux-firmware and Mesa 26.2 lists the device. */
+	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 56, 104, 183):
 		return PVR_GPU_SUPPORTED;
 
 	default:
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_drv.c
@@ -1537,3 +1537,4 @@
 MODULE_FIRMWARE("powervr/rogue_33.15.11.3_v1.fw");
 MODULE_FIRMWARE("powervr/rogue_36.52.104.182_v1.fw");
 MODULE_FIRMWARE("powervr/rogue_36.53.104.796_v1.fw");
+MODULE_FIRMWARE("powervr/rogue_36.56.104.183_v1.fw"); /* a7a: Allwinner A733 */
